t.\n- Move `buildLearningPrompt` logic into builder (as `BuildLearning` + a file-saver), and update cmd/learning.go to call builder.\n- Update cmd test files that reference moved functions (learning_test.go references buildLearningPrompt; tools_test.go/dryrun_integration_test.go reference runDoingDryRun/runPlanDryRun which stay in cmd, so they're fine).\n\nWait, `runDoingDryRun` and `runPlanDryRun` stay in cmd (task6 moves them to handler). They're unexported cmd functions. Their tests (tools_test.go, dryrun_integration_test.go) still reference them, fine. I just change their internals to use builder.\n\n`buildLearningPrompt` is referenced by learning_test.go. If I keep it in cmd/learning.go as a wrapper that calls builder, learning_test.go stays compiling. That's the safest.\n\nActually, let me check learning.go and learning_test.go fully to understand."}}
