{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The `prompt.` matches in those test files are just local variable names `promptFile`, not the prompt package. So only `learning_test.go` imports the prompt package (for `prompt.NewPromptManager` in TestLearningTemplateHasDraftDir). \n\nSo if I remove cmd's non-test import of prompt, learning_test.go can still import prompt independently. Good. The only cmd test that would break is if I remove `buildLearningPrompt` (cmd function) — I'll keep it.\n\nSo the plan for cmd changes:\n- Non-test files: switch `prompt.X` → `builder.X` (and add builder import, remove prompt import where no longer used).\n- Keep `buildLearningPrompt` in cmd/learning.go (delegating to builder), so learning_test.go compiles.\n- learning_test.go's `prompt.NewPromptManager` still works (prompt package still exists).\n\nBut wait, cmd/learning.go's `buildLearningPrompt` currently uses `prompt.NewPromptManager` etc. If I change it to delegate to builder, cmd/learning.go no longer imports prompt (good for KR4). learning_test.go still imports prompt (fine).\n\nNow, the human_loop.go and ctrl.go and dream.go and easy.go and plan.go and doing.go need to switch to builder.\n\nLet me now also check human_loop.go and ctrl.go and dream.go and easy.go source fully to know exactly what to change."}}
