kDir) (promptFile string, method string, err error)`. cmd: `promptFile, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SavePlanPrompt(...)`.\n\nActually, cmd currently does `planPromptFile, _, err := prompt.GeneratePlanPromptFile(...)`. I'll change to `planPromptFile, _, err := pb.SavePlanPrompt(...)` (3 returns). Good.\n\n- doing dry-run: currently writes file and reads it. I'll change to use `SaveDoingPrompt` which writes file + returns path, then read. Or use BuildDoing (pure) and just print instance without writing. But \"生成行为一致\" (prompts/ dir artifacts) suggests doing dry-run should still write the doing_prompt.md + debug skill. Actually, current doing dry-run writes to doingDir/prompts and reads back. To preserve behavior, I'll use SaveDoingPrompt.\n\nHmm wait, but doing dry-run currently uses `prompt.GenerateDoingPromptFile` which ALSO writes `skill_debug_skill.md`. Let me preserve that via SaveDoingPrompt.\n\n- easy dry-run: currently `prompt.GenerateEasyPrompt` (pure, no file writes). I'll use `BuildEasy` (pure) and print instance.\n\n- easy real: currently `prompt.GenerateEasyPromptFile` writes files. Use `SaveEasyPrompt`.\n\n- easy learning (after session): `prompt.GenerateEasyLearningPromptFile`. I need a builder method. But wait — is easy learning invoked from cmd? Let me check. GenerateEasyLearningPromptFile is used where? grep.\n\nLet me check who calls GenerateEasyLearningPromptFile.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_eP6Q5vSyviTs423zfH164601","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn 'GenerateEasyLearningPromptFile\\|GenerateEasyPromptFile\\|GenerateEasyPrompt\\b' internal/ --include='*.go'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1618,"output":2840,"cacheRead":156032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2752,"totalTokens":160490,"cost":{"input":0.00070383,"output":0.0024708,"cacheRead":0.000565616,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003740246}}