er.NewPIBuilder().BuildDream(params)`.\n   - `prompt.GenerateDreamPromptFile` → `builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDreamPrompt`.\n\n7. learning.go: remove prompt import, add builder. Change:\n   - `prompt.EnsurePromptsDir` calls → builder? buildLearningPrompt delegates to builder. But runLearningDryRun and callAgentForAnalysis call `prompt.EnsurePromptsDir(learningDir)` then `buildLearningPrompt(data, learningDir, promptsDir)`.\n   \n   I'll change:\n   - runLearningDryRun: `promptsDir, _ := prompt.EnsurePromptsDir(learningDir)` → `promptsDir, _ := builder.NewPIBuilder().EnsurePromptsDir?` — but builder doesn't export EnsurePromptsDir. Hmm.\n\nActually, I should keep `buildLearningPrompt` in cmd as the wrapper, but change its internals to use builder. And the two call sites that call `prompt.EnsurePromptsDir` need to use something else. Options:\n   - Have `buildLearningPrompt` itself ensure the prompts dir (call builder.SaveLearningPrompt which does EnsurePromptsDir if PromptsDir empty). Then the call sites can pass promptsDir=\"\" and let builder handle it. But runLearningDryRun needs promptsDir to print? It prints promptFile (returned), so it doesn't need promptsDir separately. And callAgentForAnalysis prints promptFile. So I can drop the `prompt.EnsurePromptsDir` calls and just call `buildLearningPrompt(data, learningDir, \"\")`.\n\nWait, but `buildLearningPrompt` signature is `(data *ExecutionData, learningDir, promptsDir string)`. The tests call `buildLearningPrompt(data, learningDir, promptsDir)` with promptsDir pre-created. If I change buildLearningPrompt to ignore promptsDir and let builder create it, the tests still pass (they create promptsDir and pass it; builder can use it or create). Actually test `TestBuildLearningPrompt` creates promptsDir and passes it. If builder's SaveLearningPrompt uses lp.PromptsDir if set, fine.\n\nLet me design buildLearningPrompt wrapper:\n```go\nfunc buildLearningPrompt(data *ExecutionData, learningDir, promptsDir string) (string, 