empts:   task.Attempts,\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tpromptFile, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveLearningPrompt(lp)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build learning prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn promptFile, nil\n}\n```\n\nBut wait, learning_test.go `TestBuildLearningPromptInjectsDraftDir` sets data.RickDir and expects draft_dir resolved via workspace.GetDraftDir() which uses cwd. My builder renderLearning uses workspace.GetDraftDir(). Good. And DebugDir will be set (RickDir != \"\" and JobID = \"job_test\"), so debug_content = DebugDir path. The test doesn't assert debug content. Good.\n\nBut `TestBuildLearningPrompt` does NOT set RickDir. So lp.DebugDir = \"\" (because RickDir == \"\"). So debug_content = lp.DebugContent (content). Test asserts \"task1\"/\"abc123\" only. Good.\n\nWait, but the learning template has `{{debug_content}}` under \"### Debug 记录\". With DebugDir path, it becomes a path; with DebugContent, content. Fine.\n\nAlso, the previous `buildLearningPrompt` did NOT use data.RickDir for draft (it used workspace.GetDraftDir() which is cwd-based). My builder also uses workspace.GetDraftDir(). Consistent.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: previously `buildLearningPrompt` computed `draftDir` via `workspace.GetDraftDir()` and set it. My renderLearning does the same. Good.\n\nAlso, `TestBuildLearningPrompt` expects \"task1\" and \"abc123\". My formatTaskResults builds a table with TaskID \"task1\" and CommitHash \"abc123\" (truncated to 8 → \"abc123\"). Good.\n\nNow, the `strings` import in learning.go: currently used in buildLearningPrompt (for table building). After rewrite, learning.go's buildLearningPrompt no longer uses strings. But learning.go also uses strings elsewhere? Let me check: learning.go imports \"strings\" at top. After removing the table-building code from buildLearningPrompt, is strings still used elsewhere in learning.go?\n\nLooking at learning.go: `selectPendingJobs` uses strings? No, that's dream.go. learning.go uses strings in... let me check. The only strings usage in learning.go was in buildLearningPrompt (strings.Builder). Also `strings.TrimRight`. After rewrite, no strings usage remains. So I need to remove \"strings\" from imports.\n\nWait, let me verify learning.go for other strings usage. Let me grep."}}
